Wiki Page tables, the width model of #828: a border between two columns moves width between the two columns and keeps the table's width (once the neighbour is at its minimum the table grows); the right edge is double, the last column's edge resizes that column and the table's handle scales all columns, both snap a width on a step to that step; a table can grow past the page, held past the edge it keeps growing (slowly within 24px, fast beyond); a table wider than the page scrolls into the area left of the text; a "Centre table" toggle centres a wide table in the editor and the view ("Alignment: Left → Centred" in the history). https://gitlab.kitconcept.io/kitconcept/distribution-kitconcept-intranet/-/work_items/836 @reekitconcept
